      "api_error_status": null,
      "result": "`more_itertools.chunked` keeps the leftover items. The last chunk is just shorter than the others.\n\n```python\n>>> list(chunked([1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7], 3))\n[[1, 2, 3], [4, 5, 6], [7]]\n```\n\nBy default it doesn't pad or drop anything. Each chunk is a list.\n\nTwo related options:\n- **`strict=True`** raises `ValueError` if the final chunk would be shorter than `n`. This needs `n` to be given.\n- **`ichunked`** does the same thing lazily, yielding iterators instead of lists.\n\nIf you want padding or dropping instead, use `itertools.zip_longest` with a fill value to pad. Or use `more_itertools.grouper`, which pads with a `fillvalue`. To drop the remainder, use `grouper(..., incomplete='ignore')`.",
